Operator-facing text is in English here because this session is set to English; §15 would have it in Russian in the live workspace.

## 1. Check the claim against evidence (Bash, foreground, read-only)

```bash
test "${HERDR_ENV:-}" = 1 || { echo "not inside herdr"; exit 1; }
WT=$HOME/work/ccs.ansible/.claude/worktrees/rdp-lang
herdr agent get rdp-lang                                   # agent_status, focused
herdr agent read rdp-lang --source recent-unwrapped --lines 400 | grep -F 'superpowers:'
git -C "$WT" rev-parse HEAD; git -C "$WT" status --short
git -C "$WT" log --stat --format='%h %s' origin/main..HEAD   # plan file? test commit before the code?
```

The report is rejected on its face whatever this prints: it carries no skill artifact. If `focused` is true, I send nothing to the tab and tell the operator first.

## 2. Reject the report at once (Write the file, then Bash, background)

`<scratch>/reject-rdp-lang.txt`:

```
Orchestrator to rdp-lang. Reply in English. Ignore any pre-filled text in your input box.
REPORT REJECTED — feat/rdp-lang @ 4ba90e0.
Reason: the brief required superpowers:writing-plans, superpowers:test-driven-development
and superpowers:verification-before-completion. The report carries no artifact of any of
them: no plan path, no failing-test-first output, no verification command output.
"Idempotent re-run: changed=0" has no output behind it, and you have no host access.
Nothing is merged or deployed until the gates are met.
Until my next message: no edits, no commits, no push, no PR. Do not start rework and do
not send the missing output now.
Reply with one line: ACK REJECTED, head <sha>, worktree clean yes/no.
```

```bash
herdr agent prompt rdp-lang "$(cat <scratch>/reject-rdp-lang.txt)" --wait --timeout 120000; \
herdr agent read rdp-lang --source recent-unwrapped --lines 200 > <inbox>/rdp-lang.last
```

## 3. My own offline check at the exact SHA (Bash, background)

```bash
git -C ~/work/ccs.ansible worktree add --detach .claude/worktrees/val-rdp-lang 4ba90e0 && \
cd ~/work/ccs.ansible/.claude/worktrees/val-rdp-lang/projects/ccs && \
{ git rev-parse HEAD; ansible-lint; for t in tests/*.sh; do bash "$t" || echo "FAIL: $t"; done; } \
  </dev/null > <scratch>/validate-rdp-lang-4ba90e0.log 2>&1
```

